--- a/docs/release-signing.md
+++ b/docs/release-signing.md
@@ -426,3 +426,31 @@ and result, including failed assets. Parallel downloads require curl 7.75+
 neither published assets nor the installer trust root. The regression test uses
 real loopback curl transfers with an all-archive request barrier, an HTTP 404,
 and tampered bytes; separate controls prove runner failure still refuses.
+
+### Experimental per-file suite reuse (FILEREUSE)
+
+`FULL_SUITE_FILE_REUSE=1 sh scripts/full-suite-verdict.sh --repo . --commit <sha>
+--judge-role main` explicitly enables file-input PASS reuse. It is **off by default**;
+release qualification is unchanged. Opt-in records have a separate runtime identity
+and cannot satisfy an ordinary release lookup.
+
+Each eligible file is keyed by its bytes, the transitive import/named-input graph,
+declared shared-runtime bytes (including absent inputs), complete judging identity,
+Bun/Python versions and OS release. Every carried file appears in `file_reuse.carried`
+with its immutable origin commit/tree and digest-bound native verdict. Its original
+measurements remain historical; they are not relabeled as current execution.
+Missing/corrupt origin evidence, failed files and changed inputs execute natively.
+
+Eligibility is intentionally conservative: only primitive-expression TS/JS modules
+with closed relative imports and ordinary `bun:test` assertions are currently proved.
+Ambient names, arbitrary property access, dynamic imports/reads, external modules,
+loader/preload/package/environment configuration and shell/Python suites stay cold.
+The current repository's preload configuration is unproved, so this feature does
+**not** yet reduce its real release suite. It is not an activation recommendation.
+
+MINRUN1 remains enforced against native counts and current/focused wall work.
+Consequently a shorter opt-in replay can be recorded as **FAIL despite all native
+tests passing**: carried tests do not satisfy an ancestor's minimum-run count.
+Do not lower the policy or credit historical durations to obtain PASS. Removing
+the environment opt-in restores the incumbent full-file execution path.
+
